    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0192" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2648</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d197-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-04T21:00:00+04:31"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                                1918, 9 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 7, 7.36
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>381. Lindley says 3,000 tons flour will arrive from England September 10 and
                    6,000 tons additional about the 15th. I hoped we would be first to report food
                    shipments. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
